.TH QSO-GLOBE 1 "November 2026" "QSO Globe 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qso-globe \- real-time amateur radio contact visualization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qso-globe
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qso-globe
is a hardware-accelerated terrestrial globe for visualizing
amateur radio contacts.

Incoming contact notifications initiate an animated great-circle
visualization from the configured home station to the contacted
station.

The application supports solar illumination, twilight boundaries,
gray-line highlighting, nighttime city lights, historical station
markers, and adaptive destination magnification.

Rendering is event-driven while the globe is stationary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Display command-line help.
.TP
.B --version
Display the application version.
.TP
.B --show-config
Display the effective configuration without opening a window,
binding a network socket, or modifying saved preferences.
.TP
.B --test-expiry
Use a 30-second marker retention period.
Operator preferences are not saved in this mode.
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
.TP
.B D
Toggle full daylight illumination.
.TP
.B N
Toggle natural solar illumination.
.TP
.B G
Toggle gray-line highlighting.
.TP
.B T
Toggle the terminator contour.
.TP
.B Space
Initiate the London demonstration.
.TP
.B Escape
Exit the application.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The application uses an INI-style configuration file.

Supported sections are station, window, animation,
illumination, network, and textures.

Missing configuration files use built-in defaults.
Invalid configuration files prevent startup.

Saved operator preferences override the configured window
geometry and illumination preferences.
.SH NETWORK PROTOCOL
The application receives UDP datagrams on the IPv4 loopback
interface.

The default port is 45832.

Each datagram contains four tab-separated fields:
.PP
.nf
QSO1<TAB>ID<TAB>CALLSIGN<TAB>LOCATOR
.fi
.PP
The identifier must be a nonzero unsigned 64-bit integer.

Callsigns must contain between 3 and 20 permitted characters.

Four-, six-, and eight-character Maidenhead locators
are supported.

Duplicate identifiers are suppressed using a bounded
history of 1024 entries.
The pending contact queue accommodates 128 events.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for configuration and operator preferences.
Defaults to $HOME/.config when unset or invalid.
.TP
.B QSO_DAY_TEXTURE
Override the configured daytime JPEG texture.
.TP
.B QSO_NIGHT_TEXTURE
Override the configured nighttime JPEG texture.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/qso-globe/qso-globe.conf
Permanent station configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/qso-globe/qso-globe.state
Automatically maintained operator preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/qso-globe/textures/earth-8192.jpg
Default high-resolution daytime texture.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/qso-globe/textures/night-8192.jpg
Default high-resolution nighttime texture.
.TP
.I /usr/share/xplanet/images/earth.jpg
Fallback daytime texture.
.TP
.I /usr/share/xplanet/images/night.jpg
Fallback nighttime texture.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
An X11 display, an OpenGL compatibility context,
GLU, and libjpeg.

Readable daytime and nighttime JPEG textures must be available.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Historical contacts are retained in memory only.

Duplicate detection is bounded and does not persist across
application restarts.

The solar illumination model is geometric and is not
an ionospheric propagation prediction.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR X (7),
.BR xplanet (1)
.SH ACKNOWLEDGMENTS
High-resolution terrestrial imagery is provided by
NASA Blue Marble and NASA Black Marble datasets.
